  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`. After the `# Habeas` title and a short orienting paragraph, the first section is `## Workflow`. Every later section (`Testing and coverage artifacts`, `Inspecting`, `Requirements, examples, and definitions`, `References`, `Gotchas`) comes after it. The Workflow section is made of ordered, numbered steps: \"- [ ] 1. Pick the skill for the task\" with a task-to-skill table, then \"- [ ] 2. Follow that skill…\". The intro paragraph is not a separate section, so it doesn't break the \"before any other section\" obligation. The site meets the requirement. The requirement lists no violation queries, so there were no violation matches to judge.",
